WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.730
.If you want to hear about the original ending
of Happy Death Day, stick around to the end

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.800
of this video.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:12.990
CZ: “Hey, what’s up?”

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.330
WD: “Someone sounds groggy AF.”

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.720
CZ: “What do you want?”

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.929
WD: “Did you fall asleep editing a Things
You Missed video again?”

00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:23.159
CZ: “Uhh no…

00:00:23.159 --> 00:00:24.390
Not at all.”

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.961
WD: “I don’t believe you.

00:00:25.961 --> 00:00:26.961
You still down to film a 3AM challenge tomorrow?”

00:00:26.961 --> 00:00:27.961
CZ: “Yeah sure…

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:28.961
what time?”

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:29.961
WD: “You’re the worst.

00:00:29.961 --> 00:00:30.961
I’m hanging up now.

00:00:30.961 --> 00:00:31.961
Don’t forget to transfer me that $10.

00:00:31.961 --> 00:00:32.961
CZ: ”K”

00:00:32.961 --> 00:00:47.120
Throughout the movie you get little bits of
information, and if you’re paying attention,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.190
you can piece some of that info together.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.210
For example, you may notice that the date
Tree has to relive is September 18th.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.710
Over the course of the movie we also pick
up that it’s her birthday,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.550
It’s her late Mother’s birthday,

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.489
And it falls on a Monday this year, so we
can use that information to pretty much determine

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:05.359
that it takes place in the same year of the
release, 2017.

00:01:05.359 --> 00:01:12.189
It hasn’t fallen on a Monday before this
year since 2006 and won’t again until 2023.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:15.640
Given that information, I tried to see if
there was any significance to this date and

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.509
found a couple of possibilities.

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:20.020
The first, is that it’s HIV Awareness Day.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.490
In the conversation with Danielle, the sorority
leader girl, Tree is given her tips to prevents

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.490
that sort of thing.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:28.632
There is even a version of the script where
Danielle tells her to be mindful so that she

00:01:28.632 --> 00:01:31.200
doesn’t contract a bacterial infection.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.569
September 18th is also World Water Monitoring
Day.

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.950
If you watched my last video you know that
I think there could be some references to

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.889
environmental preservation.

00:01:39.889 --> 00:01:43.950
Her name is Tree, which is a weird name unless
you are naming your character like that for

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.950
a reason…

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.579
Her killer is always trying to cut her down,
a symbol of deforestation.

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:52.119
Every day she wakes up goes outside where
she is greeted with a woman wearing a shirt

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:54.450
that reads “Tree Huggers United”.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:58.249
The woman wants her to sign a petition to
stop global warming, which she constantly

00:01:58.249 --> 00:01:59.249
ignores.

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:03.840
Then the sprinklers go off prematurely which
can tie directly back into the water preservation

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.840
thing.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:08.520
One of the kills literally involves killing
her with a bong; director Christopher Landon

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:13.110
is almost directly telling us that pollution
is killing our trees, our environment.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.801
Each day she only has a limited amount of
time to figure out who her killer is, just

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:19.390
as we are running out of time to save our
environment.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:20.860
And we see this in the movie.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.530
Despite the fact that she gets a reset every
day, she starts to feel the long term effects

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:26.110
of being killed every night.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.970
The doctor tells her she can’t continue
like this because she’s starting to incur

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.810
permanent damage.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.330
And then there’s the fact that it’s her
birthday, and outside of the obvious sound-alike

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:38.810
of birthday and Earth Day, maybe Landon is
telling us that each year that goes by, we

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.470
are killing our environment more and more.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:44.200
If we’re not nice to our environment, it’s
not going to be nice to us in the future.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.730
If you’re not totally convinced that she
represents the environment, just look at all

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.820
of the stuff in her room.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:52.931
It’s filled with butterflies, feathers,
birds and stuffed animals.

00:02:52.931 --> 00:02:57.340
And throughout the movie, there’s the fact
that there is no tomorrow for her, no future.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:07.220
If we do too much damage now, science won’t
be able to save her later.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.020
CZ: “Hey, what’s up?”

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.770
WD: “Someone sounds groggy AF.”

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:21.470
CZ: “...Didn’t we have this conversation?”

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.200
WD: “What are you talking about?”

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:31.070
CZ: “Are you about to ask me to film a 3AM
challenge for you?”

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.070
WD: “Yeah.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.070
You still down?”

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.070
CZ: “Sure.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.070
Why not.”

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.070
WD: “Cool.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:42.910
And don’t forget to send me that $10.”

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:46.430
There was a lot of symbolism in the movie
relating to the time loop that Tree is stuck

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:47.430
in.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.020
When she first wakes up, on the nightstand
next to the bed, you’ll see a book of Sudoku,

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.710
the Japanese number puzzles.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:57.080
Tree is trying to solve her own puzzle in
this movie, the puzzle of her own murder.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.520
And like a Sudoku puzzle, it’s something
that becomes easier to solve the more that

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.710
you have filled in.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:05.600
When she first walks outside on the campus,
one of the things that always reoccurs is

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.319
the guys who are trying to stay awake for
some protest.

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:12.290
We don’t really know what they’re protesting,
but they’re always on hour 26, which is

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.600
a good way to tell the audience that time
isn’t progressing, and the one on the right

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.489
always passes out, which alludes to Tree’s
eventual exhaustion from re-dying the same

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:24.680
death over and at one point passing out very
early on in the day.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.150
Also, on a side note, did anyone else think
the guy the second guy from the right looked

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.620
a lot like Comedy Shorts Gamer?

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.960
"It's ComedyShortsGamer!"

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:35.900
Anyway, when Tree goes to Gregory’s class,
it seems to be some kind of astronomy class

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.900
or something.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.430
I couldn’t really comprehend what the lesson
was about, but it seemed like he was talking

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:45.540
about the orbit of the earth, which is also
the benchmark that we, as humans, use to measure

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.760
and help us construct our perception of time.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:53.320
So technically, if she relives the same day
over and over, she’s retreading the same

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.940
part of the path that the earth travels, in
it’s orbit of the sun.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.370
There was a lot to take in at the fraternity
party.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.590
There was so much decoration there that I’m
sure there was stuff that I missed, so let

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.410
me know what you noticed in the comments.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.280
And I’m also curious about your interpretation
of all the medieval looking knight’s armor

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.280
in the frat house.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.180
I feel like it has something to do with the
vase full of arrows next to Lori and Tree’s

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.800
TV, but I’m not entirely sure what to make
of it.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.400
There was also this tree of bras in the corner
of the room.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.290
I didn’t go to a big college so if anyone
can explain that, it would be appreciated.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:27.280
It might just be something that’s used to
a similar effect of a pin-up girl, which we

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.020
also see on the opposite side of the room.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.060
I feel like it might have something to do
with the fact that the place is covered in

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.960
these Rooster graphics.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:38.320
Roosters are all male and this is a house
comprised of all male college students.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.780
Nick’s bedroom represents a dead end for
our protagonist.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:45.760
There are more obvious signs, like the skull
and crossbones, while there are also more

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.760
subtle ones.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:50.800
One of the posters says “tomorrow” on
it, taunting Tree on what she cannot have.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.940
There’s a large do not enter sign on the
back of the door.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.610
Not only does this tell her that she can’t
escape the room, but let’s also consider

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.450
the meaning of a do not enter sign.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:03.230
It’s something that tells us we have to
go back from where we came, which she’s

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.470
doing each time she gets killed, she resets
and goes back to the beginning of the day.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.810
The sign contrasts quite nicely with a sign
we only see at the very end of the movie,

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.199
in Carter’s room: a one-way sign.

00:06:14.199 --> 00:06:18.180
This shows up after the cycle has been broken
and tells us that time is only going to flow

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.740
in one direction now.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.180
She’s not going to be retracing her steps
any longer.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.150
She’s only going one way.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.220
Forward.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.350
CZ: “Hello?”

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:33.670
WD: “Someone sounds groggy AF.”

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:41.110
CZ: “Not again…”
WD: “Not what again?”

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:50.260
CZ: “Look I know you’re never gonna believe
this, but I keep reliving the same day.”

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.910
WD: “I’ll believe you.”

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:59.850
CZ: “You will?”

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.810
WD “Sure.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:11.730
Just Venme that $10.”

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:19.650
CZ: “Hey what’s up?”

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:24.440
WD: “Someone sounds groggy AF.”

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.440
CZ: “Yeah.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.721
Well I’ve been stuck reliving the same day
over and over again.”

00:07:27.721 --> 00:07:31.280
WD: “I mean, that’s basically what it’s
like working in the fast food industry, soo….

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.020
CZ: “I think I’ve figured it out though.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.430
I need to make the perfect Things You Missed
video.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.550
That has to be the key to breaking the cycle.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:42.350
Let’s talk about the elephant in the room.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.770
No literally, let’s talk about the elephant
in the main character’s room.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.480
A little elephant ornament can be found on
the ground in the corner across from the door.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:54.590
At first I only had my suspicions of what
it might represent, but it was more or less

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:59.350
confirmed when I heard the director refer
to the similarity to Groundhog Day as “the

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:03.259
elephant in the room,” saying that he put
that line from Carter, which compares Tree’s

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:06.509
situation to that of Bill Murray’s in Groundhog
Day.

00:08:06.509 --> 00:08:11.450
Since these comparisons are unavoidable, Landon
decided to embrace the elephant in the room.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.670
Like the one in Tree’s room.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.740
Under the table.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:18.139
In many ways Happy Death Day is written as
a spiritual successor to Groundhog Day.

00:08:18.139 --> 00:08:20.710
Both characters wake up to a song each morning.

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:25.380
Both start off as kind of nasty people and
come to see the error of their ways.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.389
Both have an arc where they try to help everyone
in the community.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:30.530
Both have arcs of experimentation.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.300
Both have a cycle where they try killing themselves,
and both eventually learn to put others before

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.460
themselves.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:40.570
The other elephant in the room right now is
the remote control scene, where Tree locks

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:44.790
herself in the room, can’t find the remote,
and the channels start changing automatically.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:55.610
It seems veryyy similar to my short film,
Remote Threat.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:09:09.820
Roll it.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:47.560
If you want to see the whole film, pop on
over here.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:51.370
You can also find evidence of Lori’s guilt
throughout the story.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.520
Nobody is supposed to know when Tree’s birthday
even is.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:57.509
Lori claims to get that info from her driver’s
license.

00:09:57.509 --> 00:10:01.861
But I think she’s lying, because she also
tries to calm Tree down by saying, “I know

00:10:01.861 --> 00:10:03.950
today is hard, with your Mom”.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.830
How would she also know that Tree’s Mom
shared the same birthday or even that her

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.140
Mom had passed away?

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:13.040
It looks like she was doing a lot more digging
than previously indicated.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:16.610
When Tree confesses to having already lived
through the day multiple times, she predicts

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:19.000
that Lori already made her a cupcake.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Roll it.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:24.180
Tree: "I know it sounds totally crazy, but
this is happening to me I swear."

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:29.810
Lori: "Tree, I'm sure it feels like you're--
Tree: "Okay you made a cupcake for my birthday,

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.810
right?"

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.810
Look at her face right here.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:35.220
It looks like she’s afraid that Tree may
have found out her secret plan.

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:39.060
Then when she reveals that someone is trying
to kill her, Lori tries to convince her that

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:42.410
nobody is trying to kill her, which is not
a logical response.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:46.620
If I were Lori in that situation and I was
innocent, I’d be asking her why she thinks

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:49.870
someone is trying to kill her and trying to
get her to safety, not just telling her that

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:53.450
she’s crazy and it’s impossible that someone
wants to take her out.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:56.460
Also, she gets way too offended when Tree
doesn’t eat the cupcake.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:00.839
Then there’s the elevator scene where Tree
goes to see Gregory, the professor she is

00:11:00.839 --> 00:11:02.070
having an affair with.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:06.480
She runs into Lori, and Lori tells her there
will be consequences for her actions, but

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.320
what we don’t know at that point is the
consequences will be death, and the reason

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:13.160
is that Lori also has a crush on Gregory.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:16.800
The most obvious one though, should have been
that Lori hides in the bathroom when Tree

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.020
locks herself in their room.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.810
That’s where we see the remote scene.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:23.500
Lori’s the only one who would have access
to that room without looking suspicious and

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:28.360
by being Tree’s only roommate, she pretty
much gets a guarantee that Tree will be alone.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:32.350
And then finally, in the scene where Tree
is locked in the cop car, Lori drops a birthday

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:35.620
candle onto the trail of gasoline to blow
up the car.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.700
The only other candle we see is the one on
Lori’s cupcake.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:42.870
It’s actually not the same candle though,
they are different colors and look totally

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:46.470
different, so that actually threw some doubt
into my mind at the time and made me think

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.500
it wasn’t Lori.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:51.279
I actually kind of thought it was Danielle
because the scene where she crosses Danielle

00:11:51.279 --> 00:11:55.830
off the suspect list, the two get hit by a
bus, which seemed like more of an accident

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:57.010
than a killing.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:12:00.350
Why would Danielle kill herself off if she
did want to off Tree?

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:04.529
I don’t think Lori was behind it either,
I think she just died by coincidence that

00:12:04.529 --> 00:12:05.529
time.

00:12:05.529 --> 00:12:09.400
What’s not a coincidence, however, are the
footsteps I hear behind me right now.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.700
CZ: “West Dakota?

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:15.100
Why are you trying to kill me?”

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.040
WD: "Hold up.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.990
I can explain.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:22.399
You know when you borrowed $10 at the underground
turtle ring.”

00:12:22.399 --> 00:12:23.399
CZ: “Yeah."

00:12:23.399 --> 00:12:27.360
WD: "You told me you were making a Things
You Missed on Happy Death Day so I came up

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:33.450
with this genius plan on how to get $10 every
single day by making you think you kept reliving

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.890
the same day over and over again.

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:38.150
And I did.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:41.910
And now I have $40."

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:47.990
CZ: "You know Dakota, like I would be about
that, but that's one of the least lazy things

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.700
that you've actually done.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.330
But I'm still gonna beat the crap out of you."

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.330
WD: "Oh geeze."

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.730
In the original Happy Death Day ending, just
when it seems Tree has made it out of the

00:12:56.730 --> 00:13:00.730
woods and advanced to the next day, as she
is resting in the hospital, someone in the

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.339
Baby mask comes up and pokes a syringe into
her, killing her once more.

00:13:04.339 --> 00:13:06.459
It is revealed to be Gregory’s wife.

00:13:06.459 --> 00:13:11.080
I usually like dark endings, but I’m glad
they changed it to what it is today, and if

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.400
you agree go ahead and drop a like on this
video.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:18.230
I really did film that 3AM Challenge with
WestDakota, so click the card to go check

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.230
that one out.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.470
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors twice a week in October, ring that

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:27.180
deathbell for notifications and I’ll see
you in the next one.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:29.830
Assuming we make it to tomorrow...

